    "title": "Man arrested in connection to Moffett Road incident - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mya Falgout ,\n1 hours ago\nEditor’s Note: News 5 corrected this article to reflect the correct age of Matthew Wiggins, as well as the day of the incident. We sincerely regret the error.\nMOBILE COUNTY, Ala. ( WKRG ) — A man was arrested and charged with manslaughter in connection with the death of his friend, who was found badly injured and lying in the middle of Moffett Road nearly two weeks ago.\nGulf Coast man accused of stealing from the same car dealership a fourth time Mobile County Sheriff’s deputies arrested Mark Flores Jr. on Tuesday afternoon. Flores is accused of the manslaughter of 31-year-old Matthew Wiggins.\nWiggins’ father, Michael Wiggins, said his son and Flores had been friends and coworkers at Austal for about a year.\n“I knew who he went out with that night, you know, but I didn’t know he was involved in it until the sheriff called me yesterday,” said Wiggins.\nHe said the two were together the night of the incident.\n“Matt went over to Mark Flores Jr.’s house for a football game, to a little party he was having or something,” said Wiggins. “The next thing we know, we found out he was off of 98.”\nDeputies said Wiggins was found lying in the middle of Moffett Road around 10:45 p.m. on Sept. 27. He was taken to the hospital, where he fought for his life before dying from blunt force trauma on Oct. 5.\n“It killed us when he passed away, you know, it broke our hearts,” said Wiggins.\nWiggins said the arrest is a step in the right direction, but still leaves him with unanswered questions.\n“You just tell me you arrested him for… you know, it don’t leave me no good, you know?” said Wiggins.\n“They should’ve buried me before they buried him, you know. I mean, I shouldn’t have outlived my kids, you know. It hurts. I hope nobody else ever has to feel that,” he continued.\nThousands of dollars worth of property stolen from Mobile home: police The Mobile County Sheriff’s Office said additional arrests could be coming as the investigation continues.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
